  "lp_spec": "tools/landed_parent/specs/pslice_c5.json"
 },
 "structural_change": "PL-PSLICE (PARENTS-LANDED 10-18, landed-regions-standard-1018): pslice_c5 (head + 7 S + 3 L leaves, r5 per-column split) as a LANDED parent: 4 clock regions h / l / t / b, each its own CTS root (PL-KIT form); all 41 cross-region nets landed (D 8, E = K = 3, +4 edges; 8,951 landing flops, 0 pads), landing halves fenced beside source / reader; 1-bit regional reset runs (depth 6). TW2-PSLICE2 real7 10-19: lp.py reader_per_inst + share_rings -> 27 rings (one per net and source region) read by 90 per-leaf read halves (6,399 landing flops), every read half + its slot-mux cone fenced on its leaf's cfg face (same offsets / D / E / K). The head's status inputs (l_fault / l_valid) are read 8 edges after its own time (lp.py lag_pins). Compiler: leaves +4 edges, reset release +6, leaf faults reach the fault port +4 later relative to command/done than in the flat cluster.",
